## Consequence

The characteristic-zero proof no longer needs to treat the entire support
graph as one undifferentiated `30,789`-square object. It can quotient the
already certified prefixes and target only the 15 transitions where the gap
changes. The first target is component 0, where support rank `190` falls to
finite rank `162`, exposing 28 candidate relations in a ternary
`190`-dimensional carrier.

## Boundary

Matching rank is an exact support upper bound, not the rank over
`Q(gamma)`. The coefficient ledger is exact over the selected finite field,
but no finite prefix is promoted to characteristic zero here. G3DX localizes
the 475-rank problem; it does not close it.

